    "Scouting Notes": "Reliever\n Filthy stuff and some attitude on the mound\n Cutter with a ton of movement and velocity in the 94 96 range.\n Fastball up to 97, though he appears to be leaning into only throwing the cutter and not a 4 seam at all.\n Changeup has a ton of vertical movement, big time swing and miss pitch\n Slider is a really solid secondary as well that can generate whiffs and he can land for strikes.\n Walks are down so far in 2022, strikeouts even higher than his already impressive career numbers\n Could be an important reliever for the Brewers, possibly as soon as late 2023.\n I don't normally go much higher with a OFP than 45+, as I view 50 OFP as a high leverage reliever. He could reach that point soon.",
